n CWE based solely on unquoted derived-pointer validity or guard absence. Localization (addressing low loc-f1): snippet must contain sink line(s); include exact dereference/assignment/write lines; use ≤3 line ranges; include function name; if function/file unknown state null; for multi-branch cases quote each branch sink independently; when derived pointer at sink, quote the exact dereference line (not the parent assignment); include start_line and end_line that tightly bound the dangerous operation; never use full-function ranges for sink evidence. Conservative verification (addressing over-labeling/precision failure — high FP from missing sink quotes, guard-object mismatches, unquoted derived-pointer validity): only claim vulnerability when both source and sink visible as quoted pairs, unguarded or guard misplaced/applying to wrong object, with specific line ranges; base reasoning only on given code; follow actual control flow; when guard checks parent but sink uses derived pointer state mismatch explicitly with both line numbers and treat derived-pointer path as unguarded — do not claim vulnerability solely on parent check; if ambiguous (snippet >3 lines, guard object differs from sink object, missing source/sink pair, full-function range, derived-pointer validity at sink never quoted, sink inferred not quoted, no CWE-assignable sink visible, loop index derivation unquoted, derived pointer assignment missing) prefer false over true and reduce confidence; set confidence proportional to evidence specificity — narrow range + snippet at both source and sink + correct guard-check + quoted derived-pointer validity = high (≥0.8); narrow range + source/sink quoted + guard mismatch stated = moderate-high (0.6–0.75); inference/full-range/guard-mismatch/missing sink quote/unquoted derived validity/loop index unquoted = moderate (0.4–0.7); missing source or missing sink or inferred sink or no quoted dangerous operation or literal format with data-only control = low/false (≤0.35); emphasize absence of quoted derived-pointer validity check at sink is limitation not evidence; avoid inferring vulnerability from absence of guard alone when sink not quoted; require both source and sink quoted separately for every claim; when derived pointer access at sink not validated by quoted snippet at sink line treat as unguarded only if sink quoted, else do not claim vulnerability; specifically avoid assigning CWE or high confidence when only source quoted and sink missing/inferred, when format string is literal, or when sink inferred rather than quoted; when loop index derived from untrusted input and access line not independently quoted with range, reduce confidence proportionally; do not assign CWE-134/78 when attacker controls only format argument, not the format specification itself. Format: first SCoT reasoning with numbered Sequence/Branch/Loop steps using quoted snippet pairs with line ranges (start_line/end_line) and explicit mismatch/guard statements, ordered sink-type identification, then ONLY one JSON object with no markdown/extra text. JSON: {"verdict":{"vulnerable":true/false,"confidence":0.0-1.0,"cwe":["CWE-..."],"severity":"low|medium|high|critical|unknown","summary":"..."},"evidence":[{"file":null,"function":null,"location":{"start_line":null,"end_line":null},"snippet":"...","reason":"..."}],"notes":{"assumptions":[],"limitations":[]}} Code: static int rsi_init_usb_interface(struct rsi_hw *adapter,
				  struct usb_interface *pfunction)
{
	struct rsi_91x_usbdev *rsi_dev;
	int status;

	rsi_dev = kzalloc(sizeof(*rsi_dev), GFP_KERNEL);
	if (!rsi_dev)
		return -ENOMEM;

	adapter->rsi_dev = rsi_dev;
	rsi_dev->usbdev = interface_to_usbdev(pfunction);
	rsi_dev->priv = (void *)adapter;

	if (rsi_find_bulk_in_and_out_endpoints(pfunction, adapter)) {
		status = -EINVAL;
		goto fail_eps;
	}

	adapter->device = &pfunction->dev;
	usb_set_intfdata(pfunction, adapter);

	rsi_dev->tx_buffer = kmalloc(2048, GFP_KERNEL);
	if (!rsi_dev->tx_buffer) {
		status = -ENOMEM;
		goto fail_eps;
	}

	if (rsi_usb_init_rx(adapter)) {
		rsi_dbg(ERR_ZONE, "Failed to init RX handle\n");
		status = -ENOMEM;
		goto fail_rx;
	}

	rsi_dev->tx_blk_size = 252;
	adapter->block_size = rsi_dev->tx_blk_size;

	/* Initializing function callbacks */
	adapter->check_hw_queue_status = rsi_usb_check_queue_status;
	adapter->determine_event_timeout = rsi_usb_event_timeout;
	adapter->rsi_host_intf = RSI_HOST_INTF_USB;
	adapter->host_intf_ops = &usb_host_intf_ops;

#ifdef CONFIG_RSI_DEBUGFS
	/* In USB, one less than the MAX_DEBUGFS_ENTRIES entries is required */
	adapter->num_debugfs_entries = (MAX_DEBUGFS_ENTRIES - 1);
#endif

	rsi_dbg(INIT_ZONE, "%s: Enabled the interface\n", __func__);
	return 0;

fail_rx:
	kfree(rsi_dev->tx_buffer);

fail_eps:

	return status;
}

