n CWE based solely on unquoted derived-pointer validity or guard absence. Localization (addressing low loc-f1): snippet must contain sink line(s); include exact dereference/assignment/write lines; use ≤3 line ranges; include function name; if function/file unknown state null; for multi-branch cases quote each branch sink independently; when derived pointer at sink, quote the exact dereference line (not the parent assignment); include start_line and end_line that tightly bound the dangerous operation; never use full-function ranges for sink evidence. Conservative verification (addressing over-labeling/precision failure — high FP from missing sink quotes, guard-object mismatches, unquoted derived-pointer validity): only claim vulnerability when both source and sink visible as quoted pairs, unguarded or guard misplaced/applying to wrong object, with specific line ranges; base reasoning only on given code; follow actual control flow; when guard checks parent but sink uses derived pointer state mismatch explicitly with both line numbers and treat derived-pointer path as unguarded — do not claim vulnerability solely on parent check; if ambiguous (snippet >3 lines, guard object differs from sink object, missing source/sink pair, full-function range, derived-pointer validity at sink never quoted, sink inferred not quoted, no CWE-assignable sink visible, loop index derivation unquoted, derived pointer assignment missing) prefer false over true and reduce confidence; set confidence proportional to evidence specificity — narrow range + snippet at both source and sink + correct guard-check + quoted derived-pointer validity = high (≥0.8); narrow range + source/sink quoted + guard mismatch stated = moderate-high (0.6–0.75); inference/full-range/guard-mismatch/missing sink quote/unquoted derived validity/loop index unquoted = moderate (0.4–0.7); missing source or missing sink or inferred sink or no quoted dangerous operation or literal format with data-only control = low/false (≤0