n CWE based solely on unquoted derived-pointer validity or guard absence. Localization (addressing low loc-f1): snippet must contain sink line(s); include exact dereference/assignment/write lines; use ≤3 line ranges; include function name; if function/file unknown state null; for multi-branch cases quote each branch sink independently; when derived pointer at sink, quote the exact dereference line (not the parent assignment); include start_line and end_line that tightly bound the dangerous operation; never use full-function ranges for sink evidence. Conservative verification (addressing over-labeling/precision failure — high FP from missing sink quotes, guard-object mismatches, unquoted derived-pointer validity): only claim vulnerability when both source and sink visible as quoted pairs, unguarded or guard misplaced/applying to wrong object, with specific line ranges; base reasoning only on given code; follow actual control flow; when guard checks parent but sink uses derived pointer state mismatch explicitly with both line numbers and treat derived-pointer path as unguarded — do not claim vulnerability solely on parent check; if ambiguous (snippet >3 lines, guard object differs from sink object, missing source/sink pair, full-function range, derived-pointer validity at sink never quoted, sink inferred not quoted, no CWE-assignable sink visible, loop index derivation unquoted, derived pointer assignment missing) prefer false over true and reduce confidence; set confidence proportional to evidence specificity — narrow range + snippet at both source and sink + correct guard-check + quoted derived-pointer validity = high (≥0.8); narrow range + source/sink quoted + guard mismatch stated = moderate-high (0.6–0.75); inference/full-range/guard-mismatch/missing sink quote/unquoted derived validity/loop index unquoted = moderate (0.4–0.7); missing source or missing sink or inferred sink or no quoted dangerous operation or literal format with data-only control = low/false (≤0.35); emphasize absence of quoted derived-pointer validity check at sink is limitation not evidence; avoid inferring vulnerability from absence of guard alone when sink not quoted; require both source and sink quoted separately for every claim; when derived pointer access at sink not validated by quoted snippet at sink line treat as unguarded only if sink quoted, else do not claim vulnerability; specifically avoid assigning CWE or high confidence when only source quoted and sink missing/inferred, when format string is literal, or when sink inferred rather than quoted; when loop index derived from untrusted input and access line not independently quoted with range, reduce confidence proportionally; do not assign CWE-134/78 when attacker controls only format argument, not the format specification itself. Format: first SCoT reasoning with numbered Sequence/Branch/Loop steps using quoted snippet pairs with line ranges (start_line/end_line) and explicit mismatch/guard statements, ordered sink-type identification, then ONLY one JSON object with no markdown/extra text. JSON: {"verdict":{"vulnerable":true/false,"confidence":0.0-1.0,"cwe":["CWE-..."],"severity":"low|medium|high|critical|unknown","summary":"..."},"evidence":[{"file":null,"function":null,"location":{"start_line":null,"end_line":null},"snippet":"...","reason":"..."}],"notes":{"assumptions":[],"limitations":[]}} Code: struct sctp_chunk *sctp_make_strreset_req(
					const struct sctp_association *asoc,
					__u16 stream_num, __be16 *stream_list,
					bool out, bool in)
{
	__u16 stream_len = stream_num * sizeof(__u16);
	struct sctp_strreset_outreq outreq;
	struct sctp_strreset_inreq inreq;
	struct sctp_chunk *retval;
	__u16 outlen, inlen;

	outlen = (sizeof(outreq) + stream_len) * out;
	inlen = (sizeof(inreq) + stream_len) * in;

	retval = sctp_make_reconf(asoc, SCTP_PAD4(outlen) + SCTP_PAD4(inlen));
	if (!retval)
		return NULL;

	if (outlen) {
		outreq.param_hdr.type = SCTP_PARAM_RESET_OUT_REQUEST;
		outreq.param_hdr.length = htons(outlen);
		outreq.request_seq = htonl(asoc->strreset_outseq);
		outreq.response_seq = htonl(asoc->strreset_inseq - 1);
		outreq.send_reset_at_tsn = htonl(asoc->next_tsn - 1);

		sctp_addto_chunk(retval, sizeof(outreq), &outreq);

		if (stream_len)
			sctp_addto_chunk(retval, stream_len, stream_list);
	}

	if (inlen) {
		inreq.param_hdr.type = SCTP_PARAM_RESET_IN_REQUEST;
		inreq.param_hdr.length = htons(inlen);
		inreq.request_seq = htonl(asoc->strreset_outseq + out);

		sctp_addto_chunk(retval, sizeof(inreq), &inreq);

		if (stream_len)
			sctp_addto_chunk(retval, stream_len, stream_list);
	}

	return retval;
}

